	'sa_s1_b' => 'Our assessor checks four core elements during the on-site survey. First, we examine the main switchboard and sub-distribution panels, measuring spare breaker capacity and available incoming load. Second, we trace physical cable routes across ceilings, service ducts, and containment trays to find the most efficient pathways. Third, we measure bay layouts, turning radiuses, and wall or ground mounting surfaces to ensure clear access for vehicles and cables. Finally, we compile installation plans and layout notes directly into a detailed technical review, giving your facility team complete clarity on how hardware fits into the existing building infrastructure.',
	'sa_s1_h' => 'What We Inspect During the Visit',
	'sa_s2_b' => 'Preparing for an assessment requires minimal effort from your staff. You only need to arrange access to your main electrical intake room, nominate a site escort or facility contact, and ensure parking bays targeted for charging are viewable. On our part, we bring precision electrical test meters, laser distance measures, cable pathway inspection tools, and photographic surveying equipment. Tomas Reyes completes the technical walkthrough without disrupting your daily operations or interrupting your workplace power supply. In ninety minutes, we collect all measurements required to produce an accurate, fixed-price installation proposal.',
