	'sv_h1' => 'Services & Pricing',
	'sv_lead' => 'We provide commercial workplace charging hardware, professional installation, and ongoing maintenance with fixed, transparent pricing. Every quote is grounded in verified electrical engineering and backed by our dedicated aftercare team.',
	'sv_post_1' => 'Serves two adjacent bays from one foundation',
	'sv_post_2' => 'Ground-mounted on kerb islands and yard edges',
	'sv_post_3' => 'Fitted, from €2,950 for 2 bays',
	'sv_post_s' => 'Best for depots and central aisles where there is no wall within reach of the bays.',
	'sv_s1_b' => 'We specify robust charging hardware configured specifically for workplace usage patterns. For perimeter parking and structured garages, our 7.4 kW wall units mount neatly to building facades or concrete pillars, keeping walkways clear with integrated cable stowage. Where vehicles park away from external walls or along central parking aisles, our twin-socket ground posts serve two adjacent parking bays from a single electrical foundation. Both formats provide steady, reliable overnight or workday charging suited to dwell times of several hours. Fitted prices start from €1,480 per unit for 7.4 kW wall units and from €2,950 for twin-socket posts serving two bays.',
	'sv_s1_h' => 'Workplace Charging Hardware Options',
	'sv_s2_b' => 'Our complete price list is clear, fixed, and published openly. A site assessment visit for up to 12 bays is €290, which is fully credited against your installation quote. Each further 12 bays assessed adds €120. Supply and installation of a 7.4 kW wall unit starts from €1,480 per unit, while a twin-socket post fitted for 2 bays starts from €2,950. For sites with constrained main supplies, our intelligent load-management module costs €640 per site. Ongoing annual service visits are €180 per site plus €25 per unit, ensuring long-term safety, firmware updates, and electrical compliance.',
	'sv_s2_h' => 'Standard Pricing Schedule',
	'sv_s3_b' => 'Installing charging points should never trigger expensive utility supply upgrades. Our €640 load-management module continuously monitors total electrical consumption across your facility, dynamically trimming charging currents when building loads peak and releasing full capacity as machinery or lighting shuts down. After fitting is complete, our aftercare programme is coordinated by Sofia Lund. Our annual service visit, priced at €180 per site plus €25 per unit, covers functional testing, terminal torque checks, cable wear inspections, and statutory safety certifications. We keep your workplace charging reliable, compliant, and operating at peak performance season after season.',
	'sv_s3_h' => 'Load Management and Aftercare',
	'sv_s4_b' => 'When you commission an initial site assessment, the survey costs €290 for up to 12 bays, plus €120 for each additional 12 bays. Once Tomas Reyes finishes the inspection and Lena Brandt models your electrical load, we deliver your fixed quote valid for 60 days. If you proceed with the proposed installation, the full €290 assessment fee is automatically deducted from your final installation invoice. This policy ensures your business receives comprehensive engineering analysis, verified cable routes, and statutory calculations without paying extra overhead for professional planning.',
	'sv_s4_h' => 'How Does the Assessment Fee Credit Work?',
